   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 6.3. Increased capacity of Member States to develop gender-responsive legislation, policies and measures for a world of work free from violence and harassment</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">To ensure effective implementation of Convention No. 190, ratified by the Albanian Parliament on 6 May 2022, on 22 February 2023 the State Labor and Social Services Inspectorate (SLSSI) and the Commissioner Against Discrimination (CAD) signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) with a view to enhancing coordination and strengthening capacity to implement the new instrument.

The signature of the MOU in a tripartite event was followed by the approval of an Annual Action Plan for 2023, which included a capacity-building program to equip both parties to enhance detection and investigation of cases of gender-based violence and harassment at the workplace.

To enhance compliance and ensure effective implementation of the Convention, in September 2023 the checklists used by the SLSSI during inspection visits have been jointly reviewed by the SLSSI and CAD with a view to include items related to violence and harassment. The amended checklists were validated during the joint monitoring visits performed by both institutions in December 2023.

To increase awareness of workers on issue related to violence and harassment, national workers&#x2019; organisations developed, launched and promoted a Workers&apos; Guide on referral mechanisms to tackle work-related violence and harassment. 5000 copies were distributed during the event for the signature of the MOU. The Guide has also been distributed and promoted during the tripartite visits to companies organized by the SLSSI and during the piloting joint visits organized between the SLSSI and CAD. During 2022, with the contribution of the Swedish International Development Cooperation Agency, the ILO supported capacitation training and sensitization activities aimed at increasing awareness about the principles of the Convention and developing measures towards its ratification and effective implementation. In particular, the ILO organised several events to disseminate the findings and recommendations of the study on the compatibility of the Albanian national legislation on violence and harassment in the world of work with ILO Convention No. 190, which was conducted in 2021. Notably, the ILO organised 6 workshops with the State Labour Inspectorate (21/06), the Trade Unions and Business Organizations (11/10), the Office of the Antidiscrimination Commissioner (12/10), the Network of gender focal points of central and local public institutions (14/10), the Network of journalists (1/12). More than 100 participants were informed about the findings of the study and road map for the implementation of the ILO Convention 190 along with the ILO&apos;s Guide on violence and harassment at work, which was translated into Albanian. The ILO also provided technical support in developing the MOU and the Annual Action Plan for 2023. 
At the beginning of 2022 the ILO supported social partners in developing the brochures: one addressing workers and containing the mechanisms to report violence and harassment in the workplace; and the manual &quot;Violence and harassment at work: A practical guide for employers&quot;, which was also translated in Albanian. It will be used to support the workers&apos; organizations in training their members in best observing the recommendations provided for the implementation of the Convention No. 190 in their respective enterprises.
The ILO also facilitated the working group set up for the  revision of the checklists by the LI and the CAD and assisted the drafting of the revised checklists.</narrative>
   </description>
